// Cloudflare Worker (with Static Assets) for the marketing site `misterr.ai`.
//
// Cloudflare unified Workers + Pages: a "static site" now deploys as a
// Worker with an `assets.directory` binding. The custom domain `misterr.ai`
// is attached to this Worker in the dashboard; this config tells wrangler
// what to upload when `wrangler deploy` runs.
//
// The actual build happens in the Cloudflare project's Deploy command:
//
//     pnpm --filter @misterr/website build && npx wrangler deploy
//
// Next runs `output: 'export'` and writes static HTML/CSS/JS to
// `website/out`, which wrangler then ships to the Worker's asset namespace.
// No fallback Worker script: requests with no matching asset get a 404.
//
// The Spaces frontend (`spaces-template/`) keeps its own wrangler.jsonc;
// the two don't collide because each project has its own `name`.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "misterr",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-05-28",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./website/out"
  }
}
